The modular structure of repeats required the development of specific cloning strategies and molecular biology techniques to avoid random or miss-assembly of DNA fragments.
DARPin, LRR and 3-TPR libraries were built using stepwise cloning approaches and for each library, a defined number of repeats is subcloned [57,59,65]. Mixtures of trinucleotides were used to eliminate mutational bias resulting from degeneracy of the genetic code.
