Artificial repeat proteins are now an unlimited source of proteins with binding affinity and specificity comparable to antibodies for any protein targets [5,67]. These artificial proteins are extremely stable, and much more efficiently expressed in recombinant form than antibodies and derivatives. Furthermore, in contrast to most natural antibodies, these artificial specific proteins can be used as intracellular agents for protein interference experiments because their structure is not dependent on disulfide bond formation.
